 3. Hochul&#x27;s AI workforce push focuses on women 
 
 By Maria Curi 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios. Stock: Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 New York Gov. Kathy Hochul (D) is turning her attention to AI's impact on workers, launching a series of listening sessions today that will initially focus on how women will experience job disruptions.

 Why it matters: Hochul is trying to balance New York's embrace of AI with concerns about its impact on workers.

 Driving the news: Today's listening session will feature several women whose jobs have already been directly impacted by AI, according to an announcement shared first with Axios.

 AI is projected to impact administrative , clerical and customer service work. Keep reading. 

 
 
